"""Older-audience pictures in the sculpted-diorama style (data/diorama_style.md = the author's mishna-diorama-style.md).
Writes data/diorama_prompts_bk3-bk5-bm1_v1.md: one prompt per picture that already has a graphic-novel picture (BK 3, BK 5, BM 1).
Fixed parts (style block, avoid line, framing lines, allowed adjustments) are the author's, word for word; the scenes are the
approved scenes of data/graphic-novel_prompts_bk3_v3.md and graphic-novel_prompts_bk5-bm1_v1.md (BK 5:1 from teen_style_test.md),
made style-neutral, with the fixes folded in and a head covering on every adult man. Run: python3 scripts/make_diorama_prompts.py"""
import re

STYLE = """Handmade sculpted figures in a miniature diorama, photographed as a still of a crafted model, not a film frame. The figures are visibly sculpted by hand: slightly simplified, deliberately stylized faces with clean sculpted planes and soft tool marks, matte painted surfaces, and no pores or photographic skin detail. Adult proportions, normal-sized heads, narrow adult eyes, mature and dignified expressions, never cute. Costumes are heavy woven fabric with visible thread texture. Settings are built as a miniature set with hand-carved stone texture, wooden doors, and packed-earth ground with scattered stones.

Lighting and depth: slight miniature-set depth of field so the set reads as small and handmade. Soft, even studio lighting like a model on a display table, with gentle shadows and no dramatic contrast, no haze, no cinematic color grading. Muted earthy palette of ochre, terracotta, dusty blue, and stone grey."""
AVOID = "Avoid: photorealism, film still, cinematic lighting, atmospheric haze, realistic skin pores, plush or felt toy look, clay look, glossy eyes, cute or rounded features, bright toy colors, comic-book or illustrated style, text, watermark. Aspect ratio 3:2 landscape."
SETTING = "Settings are built as a miniature set with hand-carved stone texture, wooden doors, and packed-earth ground with scattered stones."
SET_INTERIOR = "Settings are built as a miniature interior of a stone house with plastered walls, wooden beams, and a tamped-earth floor."
SET_FIELD = "Settings are built as a hand-built landscape with hand-carved stone walls, packed-earth ground, tufts of grass, and scattered stones, continuing back to distant hills."
# Gemini read "miniature diorama ... photographed as a model" literally and showed the set on a table (3:11a). Open-air scenes have no building to
# fill the frame, so they need this line, and an eye-level framing (an elevated view looks down onto a tabletop).
FILL = "The set fills the whole frame edge to edge and is seen from inside the scene, at the height of the figures. No table, display stand, base, plinth, box edge, or studio backdrop is visible anywhere; the set continues behind the figures to distant stone walls, hills, and sky."
POSING = "Posing: the figures are caught mid-moment, like candid photographs of real people, not posed figurines. Weight, balance and gravity read clearly: bodies lean, bend, twist and sag naturally, with shoulders and hips at different angles, feet planted or sliding as the action requires, clothing pulled and folded by the movement, and hands with individually shaped fingers gripping or reaching. Nothing stands stiffly upright or symmetrically, and there is no doll-like or toy-like stance. Faces show real age, with asymmetry, lines, and weight."
ANIMALS = "Animals are sculpted with the same matte hand-made surfaces, realistic anatomy, not cute."
CHILD = "The child has child proportions with a realistic child's head size, not toy-like, expressions natural and dignified."
FRAME = {
    "wide": "Wide, slightly elevated view with the whole scene clear at a glance.",
    "wide-eye": "Wide shot at the eye level of the figures, with the whole scene clear at a glance.",
    "medium": "Medium shot at eye level, figures and key objects clearly visible, set visible behind them.",
    "close": "Close, slightly elevated view of the key objects and hands, with figures partly in frame.",
    "interior": "Elevated view into a cutaway room, all figures and objects visible.",
    "court": "Wide elevated view, figures arranged in clear groups with space between them so each is distinct.",
}
CAP = "a plain cloth cap"      # head covering for a man, in a colour chosen per figure below

# id -> (title, framing, setting-kind, animals?, child?, scene or edit text, is_edit)
P = []
def add(pid, title, frame, scene, kind="street", animals=False, child=False, edit=False):
    P.append(dict(id=pid, title=title, frame=frame, scene=scene, kind=kind, animals=animals, child=child, edit=edit))

